  "ingredients": [
    "3 cups unbleached all-purpose flour",
    "2 cups white sugar",
    "1 teaspoon salt",
    "1 teaspoon baking powder",
    "0.5 teaspoon baking soda",
    "1 cup buttermilk",
    "1 cup butter",
    "4 eggs",
    "2 teaspoons vanilla extract",
    "3/4 cup white sugar",
    "⅓ cup unsalted butter",
    "3 tablespoons water",
    "2 teaspoons vanilla"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/zqFul132i3ZxMu3_pasOeGOOZB8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/7479-Kentucky-Butter-Cake-DDMFS-step-01-2734-10e46baebb95447493c1d76700af3063.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/7479/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 325 degrees F (165 degrees C). Grease and flour a 10-inch Bundt pan.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/iXELM_iKSzxiu52PHvpuwFy2tgA=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/7479-Kentucky-Butter-Cake-DDMFS-step-02-2737-944c0aae0ff94cfcbb7227ef21f708ea.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/7479/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make the cake: Mix flour, sugar, salt, baking powder, and baking soda together in a large bowl. Blend in buttermilk, butter, eggs, and vanilla with an electric mixer. Beat for 3 minutes on medium speed. Pour batter into the prepared pan.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/uvY6VWHwOl41xoBwhu0pqDSXGzw=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/7479-Kentucky-Butter-Cake-DDMFS-step-04-2741-61e9b58c6c1d4d20bf0f79a21e33b1b8.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/7479/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven until a wooden toothpick inserted into the center of the cake comes out clean, about 1 hour.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "When the cake is almost finished baking, make the butter sauce: Combine sugar, butter, water, and vanilla in a saucepan over medium heat. Cook and stir until fully melted and combined; do not boil.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/vgti_qggLwS2DHjZsUUJvNf_ke8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/7479-Kentucky-Butter-Cake-DDMFS-step-09-2746-c66dd7974f7e4bf09cfa695266eeadf5.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/7479/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove the cake from the oven. Prick holes in the still-warm cake, then slowly pour butter sauce over the top.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/hagEH73VmyNTlP1AOnFzEzmmlkc=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/7479-Kentucky-Butter-Cake-DDMFS-step-06-1-2750-e8bf7c9414804fceb09e1977e5bc2f19.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/7479/step_06.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Let cake cool before removing from pan, about 30 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/KRNrHMzgS7RkJLva-loYZrs3tV8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/7479-Kentucky-Butter-Cake-DDMFS-step-07-2764-cb69b84380ed4c97bf1216cad32d8489.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/7479/step_07.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Enjoy!",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/A8zH2i0Y6uWJZksOOCxmfiZ3Icg=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/7479-Kentucky-Butter-Cake-DDMFS-4x3-2809-3e2eebe249a94a85931aa1c456c548f8.jpg"
      ],
